# Curse of Predation in a three-player game: Bot1 enchants Bot2. On turn 4 Bot1 attacks with three Ornithopters, one at
# the enchanted Bot2 (it gets the +1/+1 counter, the positive control), one at Bot2's Narset, Parter of Veils (an attack on
# a planeswalker is not an attack on the player, CR 506.3a) and one at Bot3 (not enchanted): neither of those gets a counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Sol Ring
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Curse of Predation
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Narset, Parter of Veils
Island x13

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Curse of Predation.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Narset, Parter of Veils.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter#1 > Bot2; Ornithopter#2 > Bot2.Battlefield.Narset, Parter of Veils; Ornithopter#3 > Bot3)
[T4 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#3.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot3.Life = 20
